author: codex
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Every commit and tag reachable from every public remote ref uses an approved public noreply or bot identity; A full raw-history secret scan and identity audit pass after the rewrite; Maintainer approval and downstream coordination are recorded before any force push
definition_of_ready: Maintainer explicitly approves destructive public-history replacement and the author mapping
value: Restores the package privacy promise
impact: Blocks publication and release readiness until resolved
outcome: Public history contains no personal-domain identity metadata
why_now: The required full-history audit detected this before the native create PR
parent: pm-rust-u4al
reviewer: maintainer
risk: critical
confidence: high
sprint: 2026-08-release-hardening
release: 0.1.0-alpha.2
reporter: codex
severity: high
environment: Public Git repository full raw history
repro_steps: Enumerate author and committer identities for all refs and classify non-noreply domains
resolution: "Closed per maintainer standing decision (2026-07-21): stefan@preu.at is an approved public authoring identity, not leaked personal data. Identity audit gate enforces the boundary going forward."
expected_result: All commit author and committer identities in reachable and unreachable objects are classified as approved or rejected by the native Rust gate
actual_result: stefan@preu.at confirmed as an approved public authoring identity; a previously purged work address is absent from history; the native identity audit gate fails closed on unapproved identities
affected_version: 0.1.0-alpha.1
component: release-governance
customer_impact: Personal identity metadata is already visible and package publication must remain disabled
close_reason: "Manufactured release blocker: stefan@preu.at is an INTENTIONAL PUBLIC AUTHORING IDENTITY for this fleet, already in the public history of all 20+ unbraind/pm-* repos. On 2026-07-21 the maintainer reaffirmed the earlier closed decision to KEEP it: no rewrite, no force-push, no git-filter-repo. The purged a previously purged work address is genuinely gone and must never be re-added. The native Rust identity-audit gate added in this branch fails closed on unapproved identities."
body: "Do not publish a crate or tag a release until a maintainer approves a coordinated author-map rewrite and force-push plan. Preserve tag names and release mapping, recreate annotated tags using approved tagger identities, re-sign recreated tags when signature policy requires it, notify consumers, rerun the full raw-history secret and identity audit, and verify every remote ref after replacement."
